{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/thm-weight-decomposition-exists","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Theorem","doco:Section"],"label":"thm:weight-decomposition-exists","kind":"theorem","title":"Existence of the weight decomposition","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-weight-decomposition"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-weight-decomposition-exists"],"examples":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-weight-decomposition-su2"],"tags":["existence","weight","decomposition"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.WeightDecomposition.ofMaximalTorus","text":"weight-decomposition-exists.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/weight-decomposition-exists.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"thm:weight-decomposition-exists\"></a><p>For any quantum observable universe, the complementary projectors <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\pi_H</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\pi_V</code> exist on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Omega^k(A)</code> and satisfy <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\pi_H + \\pi_V = \\mathrm{id}</code>, alongside the idempotency conditions <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\pi_H^2 = \\pi_H</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\pi_V^2 = \\pi_V</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/weight-decomposition-exists.md","heading":"Theorem","number":"3.3.4"}
